---
title: Chocolate Chip Cookies
image: https://savoryrecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/0_3-81.jpg
source: https://www.verybestbaking.com/toll-house/recipes/chocolate-chip-cookies/
servings: 24
---

Preheat oven to 375°F.

In a #small bowl{}, combine @all-purpose flour{2.25%cups}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp}.

In a #stand mixer{}, beat @butter{2%sticks}(softened), @sugar{3/4%cups}, @brown sugar{3/4%cup}, and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} until creamy.

Add @eggs{2}, one at a time, beating well after each addition, until combined.

Gradually beat in the flour mixture.

Switching to a spatula, mix in @chocolate chips{2%cups}(a 12oz package) and @all-purpose flour{1.5%tbsp}(can sub 1 cup chopped nuts).

Drop by rounded tablespoons onto a baking sheet.

Bake for ~{9-11%minutes}, or until golden brown.

Cool on baking sheets for ~{2%minutes}, then move to wire racks to cool completely.